Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-15-2001||12:36 PM||||On the stock suspension in my 1985 SE on my Yokohama S306 tires I could pull 0.83 lateral g's.<P>After an Eibach pro kit, poly bushings in control arms, neg camber bushing fix on upper control arm, kyb all around, and Hoosier A3S03, and a rear swaybar I pulled 1.13 lateral g's.<P>This is before an alignment, so after I get an alignment I will post what my settings were when I pulled above 1 lateral g's.  I did not get a chance to do the test on my yoko's but I will sooner or later.<P>Also my fellow racers commented on how my car did not have body roll.<P>I also did the suspension techniques spring tokiko shock upgrade to a competitor just before my spring upgrade, and I beat him pretty bad on the track.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-15-2001||01:57 PM||||Greg,<P>Which Tokiko's did you use(Did you use Illuminas)?  Please provide part numbers or vehicles that you used parts from.  <P>THX,<P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Greg Piet||01-15-2001||03:17 PM||||On my competitors car which is a 1985 RX7 GSL-SE (same class as I am in and we normally ran pretty close in stock)<BR>we did the following.<BR>Suspension techniques(ST) springs, BIG one inch plus front swaybar(ST brand), 1/2" (about) rear swaybar(ST brand), tokico front 4 way adjustables, rear tokiko illuminas, poly bushings in the front and poly bushings in his watts link.<BR>He was also running race rubber BFG comp ta R1's (NOT the gforce which BFG pulled because they werent competitive)<P>I beat him by about 4 seconds on a 60 sec track.<P>As for his part numbers I have no freakin clue.  My parts were acquired from the Fierostore, minus the tires.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-15-2001||03:43 PM||||Greg,<P>I am stupid... I missed the fact that you did the Tokiko upgrade to a competitors ride.  Terribly sorry for wasting your time.  I knew I should not have learned to read from a mail-order product 8~P<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
